# Implementation Plan - RFCOMM IMU Activation

The goal is to replicate the successful "Classic Bluetooth RFCOMM" capture by sending the "Golden Key" initialization command through Gadgetbridge's SPP connection.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This plan requires the Mi Band 9 to be paired via **Classic Bluetooth** (not just BLE). The user must ensure the band is paired in Android Bluetooth settings before connecting in Gadgetbridge.

> [!WARNING]
> We are bypassing the standard [XiaomiSppProtocol](file://<private-windows-artifacts>/2025-12/miband9-imu-android/gadgetbridge/app/src/main/java/nodomain/freeyourgadget/gadgetbridge/service/devices/xiaomi/XiaomiSppProtocolV1.java#33-127) (which uses `ba dc fe` preamble) to send a legacy/special `a5 a5` packet. This assumes the SPP channel is raw and accepts this format.

## Proposed Changes

### Gadgetbridge App

#### [MODIFY] [MiBand9Coordinator.java](file://<private-windows-artifacts>/2025-12/miband9-imu-android/gadgetbridge/app/src/main/java/nodomain/freeyourgadget/gadgetbridge/devices/xiaomi/watches/MiBand9Coordinator.java)
- Change [getConnectionType()](file://<private-windows-artifacts>/2025-12/miband9-imu/gadgetbridge_src/app/src/main/java/nodomain/freeyourgadget/gadgetbridge/devices/xiaomi/miband9/MiBand9Coordinator.java#45-49) to return `ConnectionType.OA_CLASSIC` (or `BT_CLASSIC` if available) to force SPP connection.
- *Wait, Gadgetbridge might not have `OA_CLASSIC`, check `BT_CLASSIC`*

#### [MODIFY] [XiaomiSupport.java](file://<private-windows-artifacts>/2025-12/miband9-imu-android/gadgetbridge/app/src/main/java/nodomain/freeyourgadget/gadgetbridge/service/devices/xiaomi/XiaomiSupport.java)
- Modify [onTestNewFunction](file://<private-windows-artifacts>/2025-12/miband9-imu-android/gadgetbridge/app/src/main/java/nodomain/freeyourgadget/gadgetbridge/service/devices/xiaomi/XiaomiSupport.java#283-311) to:
    1.  Disconnect current SPP connection.
    2.  Obtain [BluetoothDevice](file://<private-windows-artifacts>/2025-12/miband9-imu-android/gadgetbridge/app/src/main/java/nodomain/freeyourgadget/gadgetbridge/service/btbr/AbstractBTBRDeviceSupport.java#107-112) object.
    3.  Initiate `connectGatt` (AutoConnect = false).
    4.  In `BluetoothGattCallback`, on connection state connected:
        - Wait 2 seconds.
        - Disconnect.
        - Toast "Now Go Scan in System Settings!".

